Z||000000||Gold-86SE||06-28-2000||09:22 AM||||<BR>What is the construction material used for the heads on the '84 2.5s?<P>I am thinking that I have a major head gasket leak or a cracked head, and I want to pull it to try and fix it.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||06-28-2000||09:41 AM||||All 84-88 Iron Dukes have cast-iron heads.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||06-28-2000||12:01 PM||||<BR>Thanks for the help Chadman!<P>Now, two more questions.  If the head is cracked can it be fixed?  And how much time am I looking at to pull the head from that 2.5?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||webbee||06-28-2000||03:51 PM||||Get a new/used(boneyard) head. They up-dated those heads and the replacements are better.<P>I find there is no substitution for a new part, in the long run you will spend more on trying to fix it and then end up buying a new one anyway.<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-28-2000||04:33 PM||||What webbee said,,,,, A damaged or otherwise failed head should never be repaired. Slight warping can be macined out, but large warp or cracking always means replacement.||||reg||1
